# DRAFT (Epic 9): the Bard's lines. Performative cadence: a beginning, a hook, a turn (narrative-design.md). He greets by
# the hour (bridge.day_phase). At the door: door_first once a run, then door_1..N, never the same twice in a row; each has
# the same three replies: "Play, then." (bridge.choose("allow")), "Not tonight." (bridge.choose("refuse")) and
# "(Walk away.)" (no choice: he keeps waiting). Raphael rewrites.

~ door_first
do bridge.mark_seen("bard_first_visit")
if bridge.day_phase == "evening"
	Bard: Evening, keeper. Every good song starts the same way: a road, a door, and a room that wants a song.
elif bridge.day_phase == "dusk"
	Bard: The light's going, keeper. Every good song starts the same way: a road, a door, and a room that wants a song.
else
	Bard: Good day, keeper. Every good song starts the same way: a road, a door, and a room that wants a song.
Bard: Here's my offer. I play, they drink, they tip. I keep a share of the tips. You keep the rest, and the road learns your name.
- Play, then.
	do bridge.choose("allow")
	Bard: Then let's give them something to carry home.
- Not tonight.
	do bridge.choose("refuse")
	Bard: Another time, then. The road goes both ways.
- (Walk away.)
	Bard: Take your time. I'll be at the door a while.
=> END

~ door_1
if bridge.day_phase == "evening"
	Bard: Back again, keeper, and just in time for the evening crowd.
else
	Bard: Back again, keeper. The road brought me round, the way roads do.
Bard: Same terms as ever. I sing, they tip, I keep my share.
- Play, then.
	do bridge.choose("allow")
	Bard: Good. I've a new verse, and it's about you.
- Not tonight.
	do bridge.choose("refuse")
	Bard: Fair enough. Songs keep.
- (Walk away.)
=> END

~ door_2
Bard: On the road they call this guild {{bridge.reputation_tier}}. Names change. Songs are how.
if bridge.deaths_this_run > 0
	Bard: I heard about the ones who didn't come back. I'd sing them properly, if you'll have me.
Bard: A share of the tips, and the room gets the song. Well?
- Play, then.
	do bridge.choose("allow")
	Bard: Then listen close. This one starts quiet.
- Not tonight.
	do bridge.choose("refuse")
	Bard: Another time.
- (Walk away.)
=> END

~ door_3
Bard: Day {{bridge.day}}, and the door's still open. Most guilds don't make the second verse.
Bard: Shall I play? The usual share.
- Play, then.
	do bridge.choose("allow")
	Bard: The second verse it is.
- Not tonight.
	do bridge.choose("refuse")
	Bard: Then I'll save it for the road.
- (Walk away.)
=> END

# Story 9.2: while he plays, E is "Listen to the Bard": one of his songs (song_1..N, never the same twice in a row), no
# replies.

~ song_1
Bard: This one's about a bridge in the east. It was there one spring and gone the next. Nobody agrees which spring.
=> END

~ song_2
Bard: There's an old tune about a pillar that hums. I've never finished it. Every time I try, a string goes slack.
=> END

~ song_3
if bridge.deaths_this_run > 0
	Bard: I put your fallen in the third verse. Not by name. Names belong to the people who knew them.
else
	Bard: Every tavern gets a song. Yours doesn't have an ending yet. I'm in no hurry.
=> END
